# Example environment for Bakery.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. Bun loads `.env` from the working
# directory on its own — there is no dotenv package to add and nothing to call.
# `.env` is on the default blocked-path list, so it is never served.
#
# Everything else about the server is configured in `server.config.ts`, not
# here. The mode flags (--dev, --threads N, --sync) are command-line arguments,
# not environment variables.

# Listening port. Overrides `port` in server.config.ts.
# Read by packages/cli/src/worker.ts.
# PORT=3000

# `production` makes `db:sync` refuse destructive changes without --force-sync.
# `test` sets import.meta.env.TEST.
# NODE_ENV=production

# Database connection URL. The driver is chosen from the scheme; a bare path is
# treated as SQLite. With nothing set the ORM uses SQLite at `.data/server.db`,
# resolved against the working directory — that directory holds real data and
# must survive a redeploy. Read by packages/orm/src/adapters.ts.
# DB_URL=postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/dbname
# DB_URL=mysql://user:pass@localhost:3306/dbname
# DB_URL=sqlite://./.data/server.db
# DB_URL=./.data/server.db

# Used only when DB_URL is unset; DB_URL wins over both.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/dbname
# SQLITE_PATH=./.data/server.db

# Dashboard plugin, SQL console: `1` permits non-SELECT statements. Anything
# else rejects writes with 403.
# Read by packages/plugins/dashboard/src/endpoints/database.ts.
# DASHBOARD_ALLOW_WRITES=0

# DASHPASS is NOT a dashboard password, whatever older material says. The
# dashboard no longer authenticates anyone: it takes an `authorize` predicate
# from your `server.config.ts`, and with none configured it allows loopback in
# development and denies everything in production. One vestigial reference
# survives, in the analytics stats endpoint, where setting DASHPASS turns a 404
# into a 401 and grants no access — the session key it then requires is issued
# by nothing. Do not treat it as a credential; do not set it expecting
# protection.

# Test-only. Unset, the live MySQL/Postgres adapter round-trip tests skip.
# MYSQL_TEST_URL=mysql://user:pass@localhost:3306/bakery_test
# PGSQL_TEST_URL=postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/bakery_test

# Set by Bakery for its own child processes — THREAD_WORKER, THREAD_ID,
# DEV_WATCHER_ACTIVE, DETACHED. Setting them by hand confuses the dev pipeline.
